<h2>Daily Office Lectionary</h2>
<h3>For Days between 4 Advent and 1 Epiphany</h3>
<p>The Daily Office Lectionary follows a pattern of readings for each day of the
  week following a Sunday in a particular time of the Church Calendar.  The only
  exception is for the days between 4 Advent and 1 Epiphany, as the holidays during
  this time are moveable (meaning they fall on a specific day, and not necessarily
  on a Sunday).</p>
<p>To find the readings for the days between 4 Advent and 1 Epiphany, select the days
  that fall between the moveable holidays and the Sunday markers of 4 Advent and
  1 Epiphany.  For example, if Christmas is on a Wednesday, the readings would
  include all readings in 4 Advent until Tuesday, when you would select December 24
  for the morning and Christmas Eve for the evening.  Then for the days between
  Christmas and the First Sunday after Christmas - and occasionally between the
  Second Sunday after Christmas - you select the readings based on the dated days
  below.  Christmas, the 1st and 2nd Sunday after Christmas, Holy Name, and
  Epiphany are found for you on the <a href="./#/daily_office/archive/references">
    references</a> page.</p>
<p>Days that are missing from these table (12-26, 12-27, 12-28) are often filled in
  with the <a href="./#/daily_office/holy_day_list">Holy Day Readings</a>.</p>
